      "updated": 1779424798948,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "            How to use Scanner class?\n            ========================\n\n1. Scanner class is available in the package java.util\n\n2. Scanner class has multiple methods for accepting input but all these methods are instance method.\n\n\nScanner kb=new Scanner(); --> object of S canner is created\n\nto accept input from keyboard we write\n\nScanner kb=new Scanner(System.in);",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "            How to use Scanner class?\n            ========================\n\n1. Scanner class is available in the package java.util\n\n2. Scanner class has multiple methods for accepting input but all these methods are instance method.\n\n\nScanner kb=new Scanner(); --> object of S canner is created\n\nto accept input from keyboard we write\n\nScanner kb=new Scanner(System.in);",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
